269
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:13,360
and we stopped again when we were in Franklin.

270
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:16,240
It was a really cool outdoor store called Outdoor 76.

271
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:17,120
It's a cool shop,

272
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:18,080
Yeah. it was really neat.

273
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:20,320
So we stopped there and talked to them for a while

274
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:22,480
and the guy there that we talked to,

275
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:24,400
who was like the leg expert,

276
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:26,000
really put it into perspective.

277
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:29,600
He essentially compared through hiking

278
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:31,040
and like the beginning of through hiking

279
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:34,480
to like spring training and pitchers in baseball,

280
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:36,400
And sometimes throughout the season

281
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:39,120
they'll get to like 80,, 90, 100 mile an hour pitches,

282
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:40,400
But right now in spring training

283
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:42,480
they're not doing anywhere close to that

284
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:45,839
because of fear of like hurting their muscles and stuff.

285
00:11:45,839 --> 00:11:47,839
So it's all very slow warm-up.

286
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:51,280
He really made it clear that the best thing to do

287
00:11:51,280 --> 00:11:52,160
is to slow down.

288
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:55,360
So we've definitely done that,

289
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:57,280
especially on the downhill sections.

290
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:58,480
It's definitely helping.

291
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:01,440
I really don't feel that much in my knees.

292
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:05,040
I have an ace bandage that'll wrap my knees in

293
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:06,640
just for a little bit of compression,

294
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:07,760
but that's about it.

295
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:11,200
Do you have hiking sticks?

296
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,200
Yes, Oh yeah,

297
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:16,880
I started hiking with the trekking poles

298
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,880
while I was a summit steward this past summer

299
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:22,560
I realized like, oh wow, these really help with my knees

300
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:24,400
And I've never gone back.

301
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:26,080
I love my trekking poles.

302
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:26,640
I know

303
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:29,360
First time I was up in the Adirondack.

304
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:35,520
I'm crawling up Mount Marcy just like the way that I do,

305
00:12:37,199 --> 00:12:40,400
And everybody going past me

306
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:43,360
is like flying along with these trekking poles.

307
00:12:45,199 --> 00:12:47,280
First time I ever saw trekking poles

308
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:50,240
was on some public television show about hiking.

309
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:52,480
Somebody had these trekking poles

310
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,560
and they're like: yeah, these are a big deal in Europe,

311
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:55,760
Everybody loves them and everything.

312
00:12:55,840 --> 00:12:58,560
And I said that is the stupidest. look at the thing.

313
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:03,200
Because it was no, no, no, no.

314
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:05,840
You use a good, old-fashioned hiking stick,

315
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:07,200
You don't use trekking poles.

316
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:12,560
But if I had had $1,000 going up Mount Marcy

317
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:14,880
and somebody would part with their trekking poles,

318
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:16,640
I would have spent $1,000..

319
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:17,120
Oh yeah,

320
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:21,280
We actually. we had that conversation today at breakfast.

321
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:22,960
We were talking about having trekking poles

322
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:23,840
and using them

323
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,360
And one of the guys we were eating with

324
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:27,600
was like, oh, I just use sticks I find on the ground.

325
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:29,120
If one breaks, I pick up another.

326
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:30,800
It's like, oh, okay, great,

327
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:31,200
Yeah,

328
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:33,760
This is the first time I've ever hiked with trekking poles.

329
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:35,760
I'm not 100% sold,

330
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:37,760
but I can tell it makes a difference

331
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,760
when I need it to make a difference.

332
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:42,000
I end up carrying them in one hand a lot

333
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,080
because I don't want to keep that movement.

334
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:46,160
Just, it starts to annoy me after a while.

335
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:47,520
It's too much trouble to like collapse them

336
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:49,200
attached to the pack and then take them off

337
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:50,240
when you're on downhill.

338
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:51,840
I don't really want them uphill,

339
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:53,120
I want them downhill.

340
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,560
Yeah Well, that's where

341
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:57,040
I mean. I have a lot of trouble downhill

342
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:58,640
on my knees and stuff.

343
00:13:58,640 --> 00:14:00,320
That's where they really help.

344
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:01,520
No, I know what you're saying.

345
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:03,760
They can kind of get in the way.

346
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:06,080
So you resupplied. how did that happen?

